From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: do not fail system suspend on a transient wake lock

pm_test on the Zero 3W: freezer passes, "devices" aborts with
  aicwf_sdio mmc2:390b:1: PM: dpm_run_callback(): pm_generic_suspend returns -16
With aic8800_fdrv unloaded, devices/platform/processors/core all pass, so
this is the only kernel-side blocker.

aicwf_sdio_suspend() returned -EBUSY whenever one of the driver's wake
locks was active. Those are short hints (the host-wake IRQ alone takes
ws_rx for 1 s on every event), so with the link up one is often active at
the moment of suspend and the suspend fails at random. Worse, the netdevs
were detached before that check, and a device whose suspend fails is not
resumed, so the interface stayed detached after a failed attempt.

Do the pm-caps checks first, give in-flight work up to 2 s to drop the
wake locks, and detach the netdevs only once the suspend will proceed.

---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c b/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
index abc8f64ed..8f2029e20 100644
--- a/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_sdio.c
@@ -446,12 +446,9 @@ static int aicwf_sdio_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	mmc_pm_flag_t sdio_flags;
 	struct rwnx_vif *rwnx_vif, *tmp;
 
-	sdio_dbg("%s Enter\n", __func__);
-	list_for_each_entry_safe(rwnx_vif, tmp, &sdiodev->rwnx_hw->vifs, list) {
-		if (rwnx_vif->ndev)
-			netif_device_detach(rwnx_vif->ndev);
-	}
+	int i;
 
+	sdio_dbg("%s Enter\n", __func__);
 	sdio_flags = sdio_get_host_pm_caps(sdiodev->func);
 	if (!(sdio_flags & MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER)) {
 		sdio_dbg("%s sdio get host pm caps: no MMC_PM_KEEP_POWER\n", __func__);
@@ -463,11 +460,26 @@ static int aicwf_sdio_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The wake locks are short "stay awake" hints (the host-wake IRQ takes
+	 * ws_rx for 1 s on every event), so one is often active at the moment
+	 * of suspend. Give in-flight work up to 2 s to drop them instead of
+	 * failing the whole system suspend with -EBUSY. Check before detaching
+	 * the netdevs: a device whose suspend fails is never resumed, so the
+	 * old order left the interface detached after every failed attempt.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 100 && aicwf_wakeup_lock_status(sdiodev->rwnx_hw); i++)
+		msleep(20);
 	if (aicwf_wakeup_lock_status(sdiodev->rwnx_hw)) {
-		sdio_dbg("%s ws active dont suspend\n", __func__);
+		sdio_err("%s wake lock still active after 2 s, not suspending\n", __func__);
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
+	list_for_each_entry_safe(rwnx_vif, tmp, &sdiodev->rwnx_hw->vifs, list) {
+		if (rwnx_vif->ndev)
+			netif_device_detach(rwnx_vif->ndev);
+	}
+
 	while (sdiodev->state == SDIO_ACTIVE_ST) {
 		if (down_interruptible(&sdiodev->tx_priv->txctl_sema))
 			continue;
